course: dictionary
lesson: 6744
title: One word, many jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word one is small, but it does many jobs. In maths it is the number 1, the first whole number above zero. In a sentence it can mean a single thing, or it can stand in for a thing already named. «Each person has one life on this earth; nobody else can live it for them.» Here one means a single life: just one, not two.
explain: Context tells you which job one is doing. Ask yourself: is it counting, or is it standing in for a noun? «Every one of these machines swaps force for distance or speed; none of them gives energy for free.» Here one stands in for a machine, so it means each single machine in that group.
explain: The same word can also mean a certain time or a person in general. «One day» means some day in a story. «One must be careful» means anyone must be careful. Read the words around one and they will show you its job.
explain: Some uses are casual. «Nice one!» means well done, and «one sec» means wait a moment. These are fine when chatting with friends, but in school writing use the formal words: a single, a sole, one unit.
fact: One is the number 1, the first and smallest whole number above zero.
fact: One means a single person or thing, as in one cup.
fact: As a pronoun, one stands for a thing already named, as in «I want the red one.»
fact: «One another» means each other, as in «they helped one another».
fact: In maths, the ones are the units place: in 23 there are 3 ones.
exercise: «Every one of these machines swaps force for distance or speed.» In this sentence, what is one doing? | Meaning a short drink | *Standing in for a machine, as a pronoun | Counting the number 1 in a sum | Meaning each other
exercise: In the number 23, how many ones are there? | 10 | *3 | 2 | 20
exercise: Which phrase means each other? | *one another | one sec | one day | one life
test: «Nice one!» said to a friend means what? | *Well done | Any person at all | A single thing | Wait a moment
test: In «Each person has one life on this earth», what does one mean? | Any person's life | A certain morning | *A single life | Several lives
exam: In the exam voice, which word means a single or sole? | nice one | one sec | *a solitary | I owe you one
